request_description:
To cover the period 1 November 2024-present:
     A copy of all lobbying records [emails; letters; memos; reports; etc] received about the Occupied Territories Bill from third parties in Ireland that are critical of the Bill or lobbying for it to be dropped or withdrawn;
     A copy of all lobbying records* [emails; letters; memos; reports; etc] received about the Occupied Territories Bill from third parties from the US, including State officials, and the responses sent from the Department, including ministerial level, that are critical of the Bill or lobbying for it to be dropped or withdrawn;
     A copy of all lobbying records* [emails; letters; memos; reports; etc] received about the Occupied Territories Bill from third parties from Israel, including State officials, and the responses sent from the Department, including ministerial level, that are critical of the Bill or lobbying for it to be dropped or withdrawn;"

Copies of all correspondence between Taoiseach Micheál Martin and the following individuals:
     Minister of State Seán Canney;
     Minister of State Noel Grealish;
     Minister of State Marian Harkin;
     Minister of State Kevin 'Boxer' Moran;
     Minister of State Michael Healy-Rae;
     Danny Healy-Rae TD;
     Michael Lowry TD;
     Barry Heneghan TD;
     Gillian Toole TD.
The time period can be limited to 14/3/2025 to 11/4/2025

I request the following records to cover 1 Sept 2024 to present concerning lobbying from Mediahuis Ireland Group as outlined in the register here: (Link)
     All records related to the lobbying event as letters, minutes, meeting notes, transcripts of virtual meetings, briefing papers or copies of presentations;
     All records of any follow-up action taken about the specific issues raised by Mediahuis Ireland Group (e.g. correspondence with the lobbying entity, minutes of follow-up meetings, any internal reports, memos, briefings, assessments, etc.)

I request the following records during the period: 20 March 2025-present:
     Any correspondence, memos or letters sent to or received from the Department of Justice and/or the Minister of Justice concerning An Garda Síochána's treatment of protestors connected with the Mothers Against Genocide protest outside Leinster House on 30/31 March 2025;
     A copy of any meeting minutes, or correspondence or memos or letters sent to or received from An Garda Síochána concerning the above;
     Any correspondence, memos or letters sent to or received from the Department of Justice and/or the Minister of Justice concerning assertions and allegations made in the Dail on April 1 2025, concerning the above;

Copies of all correspondence between Taoiseach Micheál Martin and the following individuals:
• Minister of State Seán Canney;
• Minister of State Noel Grealish;
• Minister of State Marian Harkin;
• Minister of State Kevin 'Boxer' Moran;
• Minister of State Michael Healy-Rae;

To cover the period 8 October 2023-present, the following:
     Separately, the number of phone calls received and emails received by the department and/or directly sent to the Tánaiste from members of the public about the use of Shannon Airport by the US military and/or civilian aircraft carrying US military personnel or equipment;
     Separately, the number of phone calls received and emails received by the department and/or directly sent to the Tánaiste from members of the public about any departmental contracts and/or payments to Israeli weapons companies (such as, but not limited to, Elbit Systems and Aeronautics Defence Systems);
     Separately, the number of phone calls received and emails received by the department and/or directly sent to the Tánaiste from members of the public about the Occupied Territories Bill;
     Copies of any internal correspondence within the Tánaiste’s office / immediate staff about phone calls received and/or emails received about any of the above three issues

Copies of all correspondence to/from Diageo and the following individuals:
     Taoiseach Micheál Martin;
     Assistant secretary John Shaw;
     Chief of staff Deirdre Gillane;
     Chief of staff Sarah Bardon.
Copies of the minutes of all meetings between the above named individuals and representatives of Diageo. The time period can be limited to 1/1/2025 to 12/6/2025.
